@page "/demo/feedback-contact"

<PageTitle>Feedback — Blazor Reference</PageTitle>

<div class="demo-page">

  <GupContentHeader PageTitle="Feedback">
    <PageSummary>How to report a bug or ask for a component.</PageSummary>
  </GupContentHeader>

  <div class="demo-body">

    <section class="demo-section">
      <h2 class="demo-section-title">This Blazor library</h2>
      <p>
        For anything specific to the Blazor port — a component that renders differently from
        upstream, a missing parameter, a packaging problem — raise it on the repository:
      </p>
      <ul class="doc-list">
        <li>
          <a href="https://github.com/SMEDAOman/GUPBlazor/issues" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub issues</a>
          — the best place for bugs and component requests.
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="https://www.nuget.org/packages/GUPBlazor" target="_blank" rel="noopener">The NuGet package</a>
          — for version and packaging questions.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        When reporting a rendering bug, naming the demo page it reproduces on and the
        viewport width makes it much faster to confirm.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="demo-section">
      <h2 class="demo-section-title">The design system itself</h2>
      <p>
        For questions about the design system rather than this port — a token value, how a
        component is meant to behave, a pattern that is not covered — the gov.om design
        library team owns those:
      </p>
      <ul class="doc-list">
        <li>Email <a href="mailto:gup_designlibrary_support@mtcit.gov.om">gup_designlibrary_support@mtcit.gov.om</a></li>
        <li>
          <a href="https://storybook.service.gov.om/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">The upstream Storybook</a>
          — the reference for intended behaviour.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        If a component here behaves differently from the upstream Storybook, that is a bug
        in this port — report it on the repository above rather than to the design system
        team.
      </p>
    </section>

  </div>
</div>
